<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">So inside <code class=3D"bg-text=
-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-w=
rap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">handlePriceUpdate</code>, wh=
en we tried to access <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border=
-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px=
 text-[0.9rem]">this.priceData.set(instrument, price)</code>, we were actua=
lly trying to call <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-bo=
rder-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px te=
xt-[0.9rem]">.set()</code> on <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.=
5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px=
-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">undefined</code>, which threw a <strong>TypeError</=
strong>. But here's the tricky part - <strong>the WebSocket library was cat=
ching and silently swallowing these errors</strong> to prevent crashing the=
 entire WebSocket connection.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Our diagnostic process:<=
/strong></p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Added comprehensive error loggi=
ng to our WebSocket error handlers</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Used Chrome DevTools to set bre=
akpoints inside <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-borde=
r-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-=
[0.9rem]">handlePriceUpdate</code></li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Inspected the value of <code cl=
ass=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 wh=
itespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">this</code> at=
 runtime</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Traced the call stack to unders=
tand how the function was being invoked</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>The fix</strong> require=
d understanding several different approaches to preserve <code class=3D"bg-=
text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-p=
re-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">this</code>:</p>
