<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Fa=
ntastic analysis! I particularly appreciate how you walked through the diag=
nostic process - that's exactly the kind of systematic problem-solving we v=
alue at Google. Your mention of the WebSocket library silently swallowing e=
rrors is a great insight - it's a perfect example of how external libraries=
 can mask issues.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Now, let's dig deeper into the s=
olutions you presented. You mentioned three different approaches, and I not=
ice you chose the class field with arrow function as your final solution. T=
hat's interesting because each approach has different trade-offs, especiall=
y in terms of performance and memory usage.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Can you elaborate on why=
 you chose the class field approach over <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 borde=
r border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-=
[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">.bind()</code> or the wrapper function? =
And more importantly, can you walk me through what happens under the hood w=
ith each approach?</strong> This gets into some fairly advanced JavaScript =
concepts around lexical environments and prototype chains.</p>
