<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Ab=
solutely brilliant! Your understanding of how <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 =
border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rou=
nded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">this</code> interacts with build sy=
stems and module transforms is exactly the kind of deep knowledge we're loo=
king for in senior engineers. The real-world example with WebSocket service=
 and the debugging challenges in production builds really resonates - these=
 are the kinds of issues that can take hours to debug if you don't understa=
nd the underlying mechanisms.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">I'm particularly impressed by yo=
ur analysis of Babel transforms and how class field proposals get compiled =
down. That WeakSet/WeakMap pattern for private methods is something many de=
velopers never see or understand.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Now, let's transition into a pra=
ctical coding challenge that builds on everything we've discussed. I want t=
o see how you apply this knowledge to solve a complex, real-world problem.<=
/p>
<hr>
<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5"><strong>CODING C=
HALLENGE</strong></h2>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: He=
re's your coding challenge. I want you to build a <strong>high-performance =
event system</strong> for a real-time collaborative editor (think Google Do=
cs-style). The system needs to:</p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Handle multiple event t=
ypes</strong> (text changes, cursor movements, user joins/leaves)</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Support event delegatio=
n and composition</strong></li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Maintain proper <code c=
lass=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 w=
hitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">this</code> b=
inding</strong> across async operations and callbacks</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Implement a plugin syst=
em</strong> where plugins can register custom event handlers</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Optimize for performanc=
e</strong> - we're targeting 60fps with hundreds of events per second</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Provide debugging and i=
ntrospection capabilities</strong></li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The tricky part is that <strong>=
events can be transformed by middleware</strong>, <strong>handlers can be a=
dded/removed dynamically</strong>, and <strong>some handlers need to mainta=
in specific execution contexts</strong>.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">I'll give you about 25-30 minute=
s to implement this. Feel free to think out loud, ask clarifying questions,=
 and explain your design decisions as you go. Start with the overall archit=
ecture and then implement the core functionality.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: Exce=
llent challenge! This touches on so many aspects of JavaScript's execution =
model and performance considerations. Let me start by clarifying a few requ=
irements and then outline my architectural approach.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Quick clarification ques=
tions:</strong></p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Should the event system support=
 <strong>event bubbling/capturing</strong> like DOM events?</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Do we need <strong>async event =
handlers</strong> and how should we handle their execution order?</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">For the plugin system, should p=
lugins be able to <strong>intercept and modify events</strong> before they =
reach other handlers?</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Gr=
eat questions! Yes to event bubbling, async handlers should be supported wi=
th configurable execution patterns (parallel vs sequential), and yes, plugi=
ns should be able to intercept and transform events. Think of it as a sophi=
sticated middleware pipeline.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: Perf=
ect! Let me start with the architectural overview and then implement it ste=
p by step.</p>
