<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Th=
is is excellent work! I can see you're building a robust, production-ready =
system. I particularly like how you're handling the different <code class=
=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 white=
space-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">this</code> bindi=
ng scenarios and the performance monitoring integration.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Let me interrupt here with a few=
 follow-up questions about your design choices:</p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>In your <code class=3D"=
bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespac=
e-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">executeHandler</code>=
 method, you're checking if a result is a promise with <code class=3D"bg-te=
xt-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre=
-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">typeof result.then =3D=3D=
=3D 'function'</code>. Why not use <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border bord=
er-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4re=
m] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">result instanceof Promise</code>? What edge ca=
ses are you considering?</strong></li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Your plugin system bind=
s handlers to the plugin instance with <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border =
border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0=
.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">context: plugin</code>. What happens if a =
plugin wants to register a handler that needs to access both the plugin con=
text AND the event bus context?</strong></li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>For performance monitor=
ing, you're using <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-bor=
der-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px tex=
t-[0.9rem]">performance.now()</code> extensively. At 60fps with hundreds of=
 events per second, could this become a bottleneck itself?</strong></li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Please continue with the impleme=
ntation, but address these questions as you build out the remaining feature=
s.</p>
